{"name":"Coal Hard Truth","hex":"#3b3b3d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"coal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A black or brownish black rock formed from prehistoric plant remains, composed largely of carbon and burned as a fuel.","A type of coal, such as bituminous, anthracite, or lignite, and grades and varieties thereof, as a fuel commodity ready to buy and burn."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To take on a supply of coal (usually of steam ships or locomotives).","To supply with coal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coal"},{"term":"hard","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Solid and firm.\n\nResistant to pressure; difficult to break, cut, or penetrate.","Resistant to pressure; difficult to break, cut, or penetrate."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["With much force or effort.","With difficulty."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hard"},{"term":"truth","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["True facts, genuine depiction or statements of reality.","Conformity to fact or reality; correctness, accuracy."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To assert as true; to declare; to speak truthfully.","To make exact; to correct for inaccuracy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/truth"}],"entries":[{"title":"Coal","blocks":[{"text":"Coal is a combustible black or brownish-black sedimentary rock, formed as layers called coal seams. Coal is mostly carbon with variable amounts of other elements, chiefly hydrogen, sulfur, oxygen, and nitrogen. It is a fossil fuel, formed when plants decay into peat which is converted into coal by the heat and pressure of deep burial over millions of years. Vast deposits formed from wetlands called coal forests that covered much of the tropics during the late Carboniferous and early Permian."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Bituminous_Coal.JPG/330px-Bituminous_Coal.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coal"},{"title":"Truth","blocks":[{"text":"Truth is commonly understood as conformity to reality or fact. It contrasts with falsity or misrepresentation that fails to align with the world. Truth is typically treated as a property of sentences, propositions, or beliefs that describe things as they are. It is closely related to truthfulness, a virtue associated with honesty, and to truthlikeness, a characteristic of theories that approximate the truth."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Truth"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Sub-bituminus.jpg/330px-Sub-bituminus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Sub-bituminus.jpg/330px-Sub-bituminus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASub-bituminus.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Sydney_Mines_Point_Aconi_Seam_038.JPG/500px-Sydney_Mines_Point_Aconi_Seam_038.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Sydney_Mines_Point_Aconi_Seam_038.JPG/1280px-Sydney_Mines_Point_Aconi_Seam_038.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Sydney_Mines_Point_Aconi_Seam_038.JPG/500px-Sydney_Mines_Point_Aconi_Seam_038.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Coastal exposure of the Point Aconi Seam in Nova Scotia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASydney_Mines_Point_Aconi_Seam_038.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Coal_Rank_USGS.png/500px-Coal_Rank_USGS.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=th